<title>CANADA: Derlan to sell Carriere unit for C$2.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Derlan to sell Carriere unit for C$2.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Derlan Industries Ltd said on Monday that it agreed to sell its Carriere Technical Industries unit to management for C$2.5 million.</p>
<p>The sale of Carriere, a Scarborough, Ontario-based manufacturer of wire, cable and harness assemblies, was in line with Derlan's strategy of narrowing its focus in the aerospace and industrial technology markets, Derlan said.</p>
<p>((Paul Simao, Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
